Q: Angular typeScript nested Array is not iterable? A: <p>Possible reason:</p>
<p>The for loop is called before showingEventList is assigned with an array, i.e. before this.eventDetails.getOldEvents() emits the first event.</p>
<p>Put a check before the for loop:</p>
<pre><code>if (Array.isArray(this.showingEventList)) {
  for ( const item  of this.showingEventList ) {
    this.clubs.push(item.club);
  }
}
</code></pre>

